00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:06.080
The Kingdom of Helmut

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:05.700
Episode 6
A Bullet Tour? Are You Kidding Me?!

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:02.470
Palkenya Prairie.

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:04.080
If we can develop this region,

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.920
we'll resolve the food shortages in the capital.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:12.390
But this prairie is the territory 
of an ancient dragon, Greigorland,

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:13.900
making development difficult.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.380
So that's why you want us.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:21.340
Dukedom of Blois

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:21.340
Brotrich

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.340
Only mages can withstand a dragon's breath.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.600
But just the two of us?

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.430
Worry not.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:30.270
There will be three of you, not two.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.980
Excuse me!

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:37.110
Ah, Sir Brantag!

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:40.420
I see. So this is the third man.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.760
It's been a long time.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.370
Good to see you're doing well!

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:50.830
So this young man must be the 
hero who slew that bone dragon!

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.610
Um, is there something...

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:00.710
You're even better than I hoped!

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.670
You're before His Majesty.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.830
Oh, right.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:15.230
Your Majesty, the three of us shall 
set out for Palkenya Prairie at once.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.190
Huh? At once?

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:26.070
We vow to put an end to that 
loathsome dragon for good!

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:27.630
I'm counting on you.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.010
He has incredible magic power,

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:35.500
but he looks more like a legendary warrior.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:39.760
No, that's the Palace Magician, Armstrong.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.600
He's a respectable mage.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:52.730
He's fast.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:54.790
Disturbingly so.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:05:00.930
First, we'll be going to the military garrison
 that's on the border of Palkenya Prairie.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:04.500
There, we'll iron out our strategy, 
make what preparations are needed,

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.720
and then head off to slay the dragon!

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.450
Preparations, huh?

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:11.660
I bet this means trouble for the others, too.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:18.330
Baronet Baumeister?

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.520
We just received a messenger from the palace.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:25.300
Remember how Well and the others 
left to slay a dragon a few days ago?

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:29.740
Apparently, there are a lot of 
monsters living on that prairie,

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:32.980
and there's a chance they 
might attack the towns

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:36.880
once the dragon's gone and nothing 
is left to keep them in check,

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.370
so they've decided to try 
and exterminate them.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:46.010
Baronet Baumeister and the garrison 
have been stuck with that mission.

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:47.400
Wait a moment.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.450
Well doesn't have an army.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:53.910
Which is why they've formed a temporary army.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:59.880
Shouldn't a landed noble with an actual 
army be put in charge of that mission?

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:03.590
Yeah, but they would want the land, so...

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:06.050
Huh? So you mean...

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:09.940
Yes. The palace doesn't want 
to give away the vast lands

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:13.970
they're hoping to acquire as 
a reward for merits in battle.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:21.400
So that's why they're turning to Well, 
a noble of the robe who owns no land.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:27.860
They can settle the matter of rewards with 
medals and money if it's a noble of the robe.

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:32.380
My Spinning Spear is perfect 
for exterminating monsters!

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:40.040
They're the ones who'll be in 
Baronet Baumeister's army?

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:43.230
It must be tough being the commander.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.720
Normally, Well should take up that role,

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:50.220
but when he's not around, 
his retainer will have to do it for him.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.620
Right. He'll need his retainer...

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.430
Retainer?!

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:56.890
We're counting on you.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:00.640
Hold on! I-I can't take command just like that!

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:02.260
You'll just have to.

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:04.660
You're Well's only retainer, after all.

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:06.020
I'll help you out, too.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:08.360
Anyway, it's mostly just in name only.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:10.340
But still...

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:11.890
You'll be fine!

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:15.030
No one's expecting you to 
be a replacement for Well.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:18.810
But the army needs someone 
to put on a pedestal.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:21.480
Meaning you're just a figurehead!

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.500
So do your best out there!

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:25.380
R-Right...

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:29.640
I can understand why you'd be worried, though,

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:32.100
with a ragtag army like that.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:33.850
That may be true,

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:37.210
but I think you can rely on them.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:50.370
Every one of them is a noble's 
child or masterless retainer.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:53.360
They're all hoping to earn some glory

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.820
in this battle and fuel their rise in society,

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:58.790
so they're brimming with optimistic ambition.

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:13.720
Sorry... I might be getting anxious, too.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:17.680
This will basically be our 
debut battle, after all.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:19.760
We'll be fine.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:22.740
Well's debut battle was 
against a bone dragon, right?

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:26.560
Compared to that, regular monsters are nothi—

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:32.110
Forgive me for visiting so late.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:34.530
Elise? What brings you here?

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:39.240
Priests who can use healing magic 
were ordered to join the campaign.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:41.200
Oh, so that's why.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:46.920
Um, where's Baronet Baumeister?

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:51.260
He just left the garrison a little while ago.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:56.630
He said he was going to be camping 
out near the dragon's den tonight.

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:00.430
When dawn comes, 
they're setting out to slay it.

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:04.100
I see.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:22.950
All right, let the battle begin!

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:24.250
...begin!

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:41.850
Magic Mobile Armor, equip!

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:14.930
That's the magic that converts 
magic power into physical objects?

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:15.730
Yeah.

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:17.330
On top of that,

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:21.150
its defensive strength is overwhelmingly 
greater than a magic barrier.

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:23.420
What's more...

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:26.770
is his unparalleled physical enhancement.

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:29.770
You should start getting ready, boy.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:30.730
Right!

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.400
You're not getting away!

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:37.670
Does he really need us here?

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:39.660
Maybe not.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:44.580
But his Magic Mobile Armor 
consumes magic power quickly.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:48.750
If his magic runs out on him, it's all over.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:54.670
That's why he's focusing on pinning it down 
so you can deal the finishing blow.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:58.690
Now, young man!

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:00.630
R-Right!

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.300
I want to go home already!

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:17.900
Elise.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:23.320
I was wondering if you'd like 
to join us for breakfast.

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:24.780
Of course.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:28.700
What is this?

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.140
Well taught us about these.

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:31.670
He called them "miso balls."

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:35.630
Watch. You crush them with a spoon like this.

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:37.210
Crush them?

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:40.550
There, now it's miso soup! Try it!

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.550
It's delicious.

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:48.920
I guess even the Saint shares our tastes.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:50.770
Of course she does!

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:52.660
What do you think she is?

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:56.250
Hey, I was just saying it 
because I thought it was cute.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:59.230
You can send him to hell if you want.

00:11:57.760 --> 00:11:59.880
What's wrong with that? 
It was my honest impression!

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:02.820
The way you said it sounded creepy!

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:03.520
What do you mean, creepy? How was that creepy?!

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:05.160
Hey, we have a messenger!

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:05.160
It was creepy!

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:09.580
Well and the others have defeated the dragon!

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:11.540
Yeah!

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:23.880
All right, boy, now hurry up and collect it.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.380
You're getting the hang of this.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:40.700
I was told that there wouldn't 
be a reward for this mission.

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:46.860
Not much we can do when they're calling 
this campaign our obligation as nobles.

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:53.060
But you can get more money from selling 
that dragon's parts than from any reward,

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:54.600
so it's not an issue.

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:57.770
Anyway, I guess that takes care of that.

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:02.930
But the real trouble has only just begun.

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:06.050
It's time to brace your 
spirit and your muscles.

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:10.560
But all that's left is taking 
down weaker enemies, right?

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:15.460
Boy, do you understand what the scariest 
part of exterminating monsters is?

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:18.040
Huh? There's something more 
terrifying than a dragon?

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:21.370
What was it that killed your master?

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:22.730
Numbers...

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:40.460
Elise, over here.

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:41.800
All right.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:46.630
I'm sorry, we're out of magic.

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:49.840
Saint...

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.520
It's all right. Rest easy now.

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:00.660
That's "Saint" Hohenheim.

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:03.980
We have the Saint behind us.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:08.200
Please help!

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:09.350
Take him over there.

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:10.620
Are you okay?

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:11.930
Yeah, I think so.

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:15.140
My God, I've never seen 
that many monsters before.

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:18.580
Yeah, the front line is in complete chaos.

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:22.290
The only reason we're holding 
out is thanks to those mages.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:26.780
But who knows how long that's going to last?

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:29.710
Yeah, their magic power isn't unlimited.

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:30.560
Ow...

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:32.970
Elise, could you help over here, too?

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:35.000
Yes.

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:49.950
My magic power...

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:55.910
Saint, help... Please help...

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:30.380
Saint!

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:33.540
What's wrong?

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:39.290
Um, I heard that you were 
engaged to the Dragon Slayer...

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:43.960
Man, that guy really is incredible.

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:46.420
He's safe, then?

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:48.180
He's more than safe.

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:52.690
Ever since we started exterminating the 
monsters, he's been fighting on the front line.

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:56.390
Honestly, we've only been able to 
hold out this long because of him.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:16:00.640
At this point, he's bolstering 
the spirits of the entire army.

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.020
He really is a hero, that Dragon Slayer!

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:04.880
I see.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:09.570
Born heroes really are different 
from the rest of us.

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:19.580
Even today, part of me is wondering 
if I'm actually acting like a hero.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:23.760
I'm not even that brave.

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.310
Saint...

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:49.860
<i>He is still pretending to be our hero.</i>

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:52.970
<i>So I must also...</i>

00:16:56.770 --> 00:16:58.060
Saint...

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:01.120
Thank you so much.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:09.780
Excuse me!

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:12.920
Please give me medical tools, too.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:15.900
Here.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.200
Thank you.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:21.220
I've used up all of my magic power.

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:23.330
But there's still more I can—

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:24.810
A messenger!

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:28.020
The troops are returning from the front line!

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.070
We won...

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:34.940
We won!

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:43.440
Rescue team!

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:46.320
Please come at once!

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:48.830
Sir Baumeister has been 
carried here with an injury!

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:01.180
Baronet Baumeister!

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:05.660
Elise?

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.330
Elise? Elise?!

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:26.310
Oh, don't force yourself.

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:30.080
No, I'm fine now.

00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:34.290
I heard many stories about 
you on the front line.

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:34.930
Huh?

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:38.370
One of the older soldiers 
who had been badly hurt said,

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:42.560
"I was rescued by the Saint 
at the medical tents."

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:48.980
"We have the Saint on our side, 
so we can be strong and fight again."

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:52.670
Everyone was able to fight until the very end

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:56.450
because of all your hard work as the Saint.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:57.430
Thank you.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.530
Oh, wait here. I'll bring you some water.

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:13.380
Elise?

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:18.010
You're not a hero.

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:19.690
That's just...

00:19:24.340 --> 00:19:30.390
I understand that you're not some hero...

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:48.280
My niece! I'm sorry we worried you!

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:50.380
Huh? Niece?!

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:53.480
What, you didn't know?

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:56.170
Elise is the magician's niece.

00:19:56.820 --> 00:20:02.130
What?!

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:20.620
Huh?

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:21.970
W-Wait, w-wait, wait!

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:23.560
When was this made?!

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:26.130
Huh? When you were promoted to baron.

00:20:26.130 --> 00:20:26.720
See?

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:29.020
There are two medals.

00:20:31.110 --> 00:20:33.540
Forget about that. Just bring our stuff in.

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:39.370
I can't believe we wound 
up staying in the capital.

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:42.020
Duke Bleichröder's way too dense.

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:47.910
Calling for a continuation of our training 
in the capital at this point in time...

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:51.450
Sir Wendelin, does the miso go in the kitchen?

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:54.230
I'll carry that, Elise.

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:58.430
I guess they would start 
living together after that.

00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:02.050
Trying to appeal to him in front 
of his official wife seems a little...

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:05.110
This is the worst crisis for 
Operation Concubine Seduction!

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:08.810
That reminds me, there is one 
thing I wanted to ask you.

00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:09.700
What's that?

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:17.080
I was under the impression that you were 
already engaged to Iina and Louise.

00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:21.750
N-No, I'm not.

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:23.240
I see.

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:25.720
I just assumed you were, 
since you were living together.

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:28.090
What about you, Elise?

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:31.180
I mean, how do you feel about... concubines?

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:34.390
I think it's perfectly normal.

00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:38.130
<i>That's the same businesslike 
response everyone else gives me.</i>

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:40.110
Then we'd like to marry you, too!

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:42.090
What?!

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:44.780
<i>I feel like this moment is our only chance!</i>

00:21:45.060 --> 00:21:48.530
<i>This is biggest turning point in 
Operation Concubine Seduction!</i>

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:56.750
